## PROJECT-SPECIFIC CONTEXT

This project is a Next.js + TypeScript codebase using Jest for testing and react-hook-form for
form handling. The target of this ticket is src/components/pages/CheckoutPage, a sensitive surface
that handles email input and confirmation. Email case sensitivity is a common trap in validation
logic: email addresses are case-insensitive per RFC 5321, so comparisons must normalize. Check
whether any brief proposes handling this via simple string equality rather than case-folding or
dedicated email comparison.

All commits must pass: (1) `npx lint-staged` (runs linters on staged files), and (2) branch name
validation against `^(feature|bugfix|tech|release|hotfix)/[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+(/[a-z0-9-]+)?$`. The
current branch is `bugfix/AI-AMSD-2041`. Tests are run via `npm run test` (jest); coverage checks
use `npm run test:coverage-check`, which requires `npm run build:config` as a pretest step. Any
brief that proposes code without a test must declare why, or it is a defect.

Where a finding turns on whether a named dependency or path is present in a codeline, fill in
the verification field as well as writing the prose. The pipeline re-runs that exact check
against the repository and DISCARDS any finding the check refutes — so a careless reading
costs nothing, and a correct one is confirmed independently of how convincingly you argued it.

